    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0487" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg371"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/687.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Minister to the Dominican
                        Republic</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 17, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>As to the expressed desire of the Dominican Government to communicate; its reply
                    to the note directly to the President, the cable <pb facs="0488" n="372"
                        xml:id="pg372"/> service is most unsatisfactory and the Department is
                    convinced that such a course would result merely in unnecessary delay,
                    detrimental to the interests of both countries. You will say to the Dominican
                    Government that the President directs me to reply that he would much prefer that
                    all its communications be transmitted through the usual channel, in order to
                    expedite in every possible way this matter, which is of such great urgency. You
                    will also state that the terms of the note and the date finally fixed for the
                    Legation’s presentation thereof were determined by the personal direction of the
                    President.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
